ATE x 1 4cm portion of gray to tan pink  fibroadipose tissue containing a localization wire  A short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long stitch the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal dense  diffusely gritty  gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received separate in the specimen container are two tan red portions of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  Both fragments are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal focally gritty dense  gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions  A metal clip is not identified  The larger fragment is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the smaller as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electron