ial sections of the medial margins are submitted in cassettes E and F  showing the extension of fibrous tissue against the inked margin  A representative section of the fibrous tissue against the inferior margin is submitted in cassette G  Section containing the deep  posterior  margin with a small fibrous region on the inferior margin is submitted in cassette H  An additional section of the mass near the medial half is submitted in I  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary content   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 7cm in diameter  submitted in cassettes J through M  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 MAY 94 at 13 33 CLINICAL DATA  History of breast trauma five months ago   chronic hematoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   3 5 CM   HIGH GRADE  FOCALLY PRESENT MUCH LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE RESECTION MARGIN  NOTE  No definitive in situ component is seen  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is present  Some features resemble that of medullary carcinoma  however  the infiltrative growth pattern  focal tubule formation and sparce lymphoplasmacytic response favors the diagnosis of an infiltrating ductal carcinoma  The results of stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 94 at 14 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm mass  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm centrally located soft  tan  well defined mass with a central cystic degeneration and hemorrhage with a closest margin being 0 1cm away  SECTION CODE  A E  representative tumor F H  representative surrounding tissue  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  POSSIBLY MEDULLARY  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , No.
