g the axillary tail   There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm skin ellipse that has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm brown  nodule in the medial aspect  0 6cm from the closest skin margin  The areola  appears unremarkable  the nipple is retracted  The anterior margin is inked  blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x  1 2 x 0 6cm tan  firm stellate nodule in the upper inner quadrant at  approximately 2 o clock  This nodule is located 0 9cm from the posterior  margin and 1 2cm from the anterior margin and is referred to as mass  1  REMOVED_DATE  cm inferior to mass  1 and extending laterally is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1 6cm irregular  nodular lesion  this will now be referred to as mass  2  which appears to  extend along the fibrous bands  Mass  2 extends 7 slices lateral of mass  1   Mass  2 is 0 5cm from the anterior margin and is adjacent to the posterior  margin  It appears to extend into the nipple  In addition  there is a 0 3cm  in diameter firm nodule at 12 o clock  located 0 6cm from the anterior margin   2 5cm from the posterior margin  and 2 5cm from mass  2  The remainder of  the breast parenchyma is unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  No lymph nodes are  identified in the lateral most portion  Representative sections are submitted  as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to closest anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to closest posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section mass  1 to posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section just inferior to mass  1  intervening section between mass  1 to  mass  2     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass  2 from 1st slice adjacent to slice  containing both mass  1 and mass  2    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass  2 from 2nd slice    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from 3rd slice   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains representative  sections of   papillary involvement   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains