rogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and un it number  are five separate parts  Labeled  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast biopsy  two short suture designating the superior aspect  a long suture designating the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked black  with anterior  superficial  surface inked blue over black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal white  firm  dense tissue  most adjacent to the superior and lateral resection margins  The area of firmness has irregular  stellate configuration scattered with white spicules and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in maximal cross section  Section code  A H  representative sections  from medial to lateral Labeled  left breast tissue  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of breast tissue  The tissue is oriented with a short stitch designating its superomedial portion  a long stitch designating the inferolateral aspect and a double stitch designating the superior aspect  that represents the new resection margin  The new resection margin is inked black  the opp