ast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  4 x 17 x 22cm  containing a REMOVED_DATE x 18cm skin ellipse which includes a 3 x 3cm slightly eccentric nipple  The deep margin of the specimen is inked black and the specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 2 x 2 x 2 5cm firm  ill defined  tan pink area which measures 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  Representative section of the tumor with the closest  deep  margin is submitted in cassette K  Representative areas of the tumor in L through N  Representative unremarkable breast away from the mass are submitted in O and P  The axillary tail measures 5 x 7 x 10cm in overall dimensions  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes Q through T  Labeled  upper lateral flap  left breast  are two fragments of adipose tissue measuring 2 x 3 x 3cm in overall dimension  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue and submitted entirely in cassettes U through X  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , No.
