Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 93 at 13 55 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  1   OCCUPY A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  99   INVOLVING DUCTS AND LOBULES THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN AND EXTENDING TO MANY MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 93 at 12 52                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1  in scant invasive component  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The specimen submitted for BRDU consists primarily of in situ  and scant amounts of invasive carcinoma  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 93 at 16 41     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Negative  Progestin receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma is not recognized in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire in place  Sectioning reveals many small areas of yellow calcification and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan gray  poorly defined area  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1  The suspicious area is submitted in A through D  the remainder entirely in E through K  Resident  George O  Kucyj  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LE